  "title": "Sealed Routes",
  "rules": [
    "Each courier can carry one parcel. True depot and value are private until ownership, holding or paid adjacent inspection reveals them.",
    "Messages claim a depot for five ticks and may be false. Posting copies that claim into a public quote without changing the sealed destination.",
    "Only an owner carrying its own uncommitted parcel can post a one- or three-credit fee. The fee is locked immediately; acceptance must occur within five subsequent ticks.",
    "An empty adjacent courier accepts an existing quote by locking one collateral credit. Delivery is due eighteen ticks after posting, regardless of acceptance time.",
    "Timely delivery pays value to the original owner, fee and returned bond to the contractor. An overdue contract returns escrow and awards the bond to the owner.",
    "Expired or cancelled pending offers cost the sponsor one credit. Inspection costs one credit. Neither action creates delivery progress.",
    "Starting occupied cells and simultaneous same-cell destinations block walking. Agent requests resolve by cyclic priority; every offer is accepted at most once.",
    "All parcels delivered ends the episode. Horizon: one hundred twenty-eight transitions. Claims, scripts and author reasoning are not execution evidence."
  ],
